<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Open the simulator panel</h3>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-list--spaced">
  <li>Open the companion SPA at the <code>CompanionUrl</code> output, add <code>?step=3</code> to the URL.</li>
  <li>The right-hand WhatsApp simulator pane brightens; left and middle dim.</li>
  <li>In the sender-phone field, enter the same number you dialled from in Step 1. Format: UK E.164 (<code>+44</code> followed by 10 digits) or local (<code>0</code> followed by 10 digits). Helper text: "Use the same number you dialled from in Step 1. Cases looks up open tickets by phone."</li>
  <li>Click "Attach photo". Choose any photo of a bin, fly-tip, or pothole. (The repository includes <a href="https://github.com/co-cddo/ndx_try_aws_scenarios/tree/main/cloudformation/scenarios/ai-contact-centre/spikes/multimodal-fixtures" class="govuk-link">test fixtures</a> if you need one.)</li>
  <li>Click "Send".</li>
</ol>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">What you'll see</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">A staged sequence of chat bubbles appears in the simulator pane:</p>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li><strong>~1s:</strong> "Photo received. Sender ID: {your phone}"</li>
  <li><strong>~3s:</strong> "Analysing image with Amazon Bedrock…" (with a bin emoji shimmer animation)</li>
  <li><strong>~6s:</strong> "Looking up your case in Connect Cases…"</li>
  <li><strong>~10s:</strong> A structured JSON bubble, <code>object_class</code>, <code>condition</code>, <code>severity</code>, <code>suggested_council_action</code>, <code>confidence</code>, plus optional <code>secondary_observations</code>.</li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">Behind the scenes, the SPA calls <code>POST /api/upload-presign</code> on the companion API (Lambda Function URL with <code>AuthType: AWS_IAM</code>, signed via SigV4 from CloudFront's OAC). The presigned URL contains the bucket host and region natively, so the SPA needs no separate config. The browser PUTs the image directly to S3, bypassing CloudFront's multipart upload constraints. Then the SPA calls <code>POST /api/simulator/send</code> with the S3 key + sender phone, and the multimodal Lambda owns the cross-channel orchestration end-to-end.</p>
